WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.150
A ball sits high on a valley.

2
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.280
One step can walk it down, or

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:07.760
throw it out the other side.

4
00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:12.890
Today: loss, the gradient, and why a step

5
00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.710
that is too big climbs out of the valley.

6
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.740
The loss is a number that is large

7
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.420
when the answer is wrong.

8
00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:23.730
Learning picks weights that

9
00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.010
make that number small.

10
00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:28.990
The gradient points uphill, locally.

11
00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:32.720
Descent steps the other way, against it.

12
00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:35.990
For the loss theta squared,

13
00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.370
the slope is two theta.

14
00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.810
At three, with a rate of a tenth, the

15
00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:43.670
next value is two point four.

16
00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.690
Here the ball takes steps

17
00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:48.010
down theta squared.

18
00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.400
A small rate crawls, and a rate

19
00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.120
that is too big climbs out.

20
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:54.880
Quick check!

21
00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:58.680
The loss is theta squared, theta is

22
00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:01.060
two, and the rate is a quarter.

23
00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.200
Where is theta after one step?

24
00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:05.780
At one.

25
00:01:06.430 --> 00:01:08.310
The slope is four, and a

26
00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:09.730
quarter of four is one.

27
00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.650
In the app, open the Gradient descent lab.

28
00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:17.350
Run a good step, then a step that is

29
00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:19.590
too big, and watch the ball.

30
00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:21.550
Your turn.

31
00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:24.390
The loss grows on every step.

32
00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:26.750
What is the most likely cause?

33
00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:28.960
Remember this.

34
00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:32.140
The gradient points uphill, and

35
00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:33.920
the size of the step decides

36
00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.580
whether you stay in the valley.

37
00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:38.140
Try it on paper tonight.

38
00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.600
Take the step from three, at a rate of a

39
00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.140
tenth, and write two point four.
